  "term": "mental examination",
  "definition": "In this historical legal-psychiatric context, a mental examination means a personal assessment of an accused person’s mental state before trial. The passage presents it as a medico-legal inquiry that could raise concern if it led to a confession and so affected criminal proceedings.",
